      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,-2),(2,-2)$ and $(2,2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-2)}=(-1)\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{(-1)}=4, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=(-1)\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{(2)}=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,2)}=(-1)\\frac{(2)^{2}}{(2)}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](24a6feca87c2fc654fe9b1129b02dfc56d708553329bf24748dfbb27c835f0c2.png)",
